    <selectionEntry id="eb0a-2c5d-17fd-d1ba-bf89a" name="* Deimos Pattern Vindicator Laser Destroyer" hidden="true" collective="false" type="upgrade">
      <profiles>
        <profile id="7a87-05c6-5887-2f68-bf89a" name="Laser Destroyer Array" hidden="false" typeId="d5f97c0b-9fc9-478d-aa34-a7c414d3ea48">
          <profiles />
          <rules />
          <infoLinks />
          <modifiers />
          <characteristics>
            <characteristic name="Range" typeId="6fa97fa8-ea74-4a27-a0fb-bc4e5f367464">48</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Strength" typeId="a6383362-5aa8-4ff0-b1d0-00e059fc9d45">9</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="AP" typeId="6abee736-f8d3-498e-97ac-a5c68445609f">2</characteristic>
            <characteristic name="Type" typeId="077c342f-d7b9-45c6-b8af-88e97cafd3a2">Ordnance 1, Twin-linked </characteristic>
          </characteristics>
        </profile>
      </profiles>
      <rules>
        <rule id="5d75-cc3e-62a9-0f84-bf89a" name="Power Capacitator" hidden="false">
          <profiles />
          <rules />
          <infoLinks />
          <modifiers />
          <description>The vehicle's internal volume, which is normally taken up with a munitions store for the more common Vindicator's demolisher cannon, is instead occupied by a bulky reactor-charged power capacitor whose energy stores can be used to greatly increase 
the laser destroyer's rate of fire. Stability is required for this overcharged firing however, and it is possible for the capacitor to overload the vehicle's energy grid with disastrous consequences.</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="ea93-11e2-6cb6-7230-bf89a" name="Capacitator Fire" hidden="false">
          <profiles />
          <rules />
          <infoLinks />
          <modifiers />
          <description> If the Vindicator Tank Destroyer has not moved this turn, the laser destroyer array becomes an Ordnance 2, Twin-linked weapon</description>
        </rule>
        <rule id="07f5-064c-8950-9703-bf89a" name="Overcharged Fire" hidden="false">
          <profiles />
          <rules />
          <infoLinks />
          <modifiers />
          <description>The owning player may declare an overcharged volley if the vehicle has not moved this turn, in which case the laser destroyer array becomes Ordnance 3, Twin-linked. However, after the weapon is fired in this mode, roll a D6. On a roll of a 1, the Vindicator suffers a single Hull Point of damage.</description>
        </rule>
      </rules>
      <infoLinks>
        <infoLink id="2fe4-24b0-1200-45f4-bf89a" hidden="false" targetId="261b-5bb5-42b6-a0ef-bf89a" type="profile">
